    What the logon-time reconnect does NOT get:

      Windows reconnects mapped drives early in the logon sequence. A
      tunnel that comes up as a service is not carrying traffic yet at
      that moment, so the reconnect fails and the drive is recorded
      Unavailable. Windows does not retry it afterwards.

      Measured 2m23s after boot: 445 reachable, credential present,
      drive still Unavailable and not attached to the session.

